# One line-ending convention, everywhere: LF in the index and LF in the working tree, on Windows,
# the Mac and Linux alike. The templates get copied into other repos, so a CRLF that slipped in
# here would travel into every one of them. And sprinter.py starts with a shebang line: with a
# CRLF on it, ./scripts/sprinter.py fails with "No such file or directory" for an interpreter
# named python3\r.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never converted, never diffed as text. `text=auto` already detects these, but saying
# it out loud costs nothing and survives a file that fools the heuristic.
*.png binary
*.PNG binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
